  "readme": {
    "path": "README.md",
    "sha256": "10447f1839657020110fca80c630041cae09f1e9db9755cb25059846d39e2ef1",
    "characters_read": 642,
    "excerpt": "# python-docx *python-docx* is a Python library for reading, creating, and updating Microsoft Word 2007+ (.docx) files. ## Installation ``` pip install python-docx ``` ## Example ```python >>> from docx import Document >>> document = Document() >>> document.add_paragraph(\"It was a dark and stormy night.\") <docx.text.paragraph.Paragraph object at 0x10f19e760> >>> document.save(\"dark-and-stormy.docx\") >>> document = Document(\"dark-and-stormy.docx\") >>> document.paragraphs[0].text 'It was a dark and stormy night.' ``` More information is available in the [python-docx documentation](https://python-docx.readthedocs.org/en/latest/)",
    "source_url": "https://github.com/python-openxml/python-docx/blob/e45454602b53e8e572b179ccf1c91093ec9f4ed7/README.md",
    "edition_flags": []
